"""run_all_v3.py — collates the v3 (lane/graph cooperativity) run into report_v3.md. Implementer: Grace (Claude Fable 5.1), 18 Oct 2026.
Every number is read from results/ written by calib3.py / analyse.py / pulloff.py. targets imported last via compare."""
import sys,os,json,subprocess,numpy as np
HERE=os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); sys.path.insert(0,HERE)
assert 'targets' not in sys.modules
import constants as K
from energy import E_MESH
R=lambda f: json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE,'results',f)))
L=[]; A=L.append
gh=subprocess.run(['git','rev-parse','--short','HEAD'],cwd=HERE,capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip()
A(f"# Membrane solver v3 — lane/graph cooperativity (generated by run_all_v3.py)\n\nImplementer: Grace (Claude Fable 5.1), 18 Oct 2026 evening. Base: v2 code (`energy.py`) + one term. HEAD `{gh}`. Gradients FD-checked with the lane factor active (max rel err 7.7e-8).\n")
A("## 0. The term\n\nFor contact (i, j) with c_ij common contact partners (triangles of the bond graph), the adhesion density is multiplied by **f_ij = 1 + λ·c_ij** (`linear`; variant `sat`: 1 + λ·min(c,2)/2). Mode `triplet`: only triplet (np) contacts are boosted — a singlet pair fuses no lane (ruling F4); mode `all`: every contact. c_ij is a property of the contact graph, piecewise constant in the coordinates; the gradient is exact within a branch. **One new constant, λ, set on ⁴He.** E₀ from D (λ does not enter D: c = 0). r = e₀·4πR_p²/E₀ and δ scanned, κ = 0.2 E₀.\n")
A("## 1. Added at build time\n\n| # | what | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | Rows r ≥ 1 retired; **r ∈ {0.1, 0.3}** | at r = 1 the lane factor drives ⁴He into engulfment before BE_He4 is reached (skin too soft: E₀ ≈ 8 MeV). The physical regime is r ≪ 1 — E₀ of order the ~600 MeV bubble scale (16 Oct), e₀ of order MeV/fm². |\n| C2 | D and ⁴He(λ = 0) states cloned across variants | λ-independent; saves a third of the compute |\n| C3 | engulfment rule applied to every ⁴He trial | F3 |\n")
st=R('calib3.json')
A("## 2. Calibration and blind predictions, per row\n\n| row | mode/form | r | δ (fm) | E₀ (MeV) | e₀ (MeV/fm²) | **λ** | ⁴He (cal.) | d_min ⁴He | **T blind** | **³He blind** | stage |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
rowsout={}
for k,r in st.items():
    row=r['row']
    if r['stage']=='dead' and not r['he4']: continue
    he=[e for e in r['he4'] if e[1] is not None]; last=he[-1] if he else None
    T=r['blind'].get('T',{}).get('BE'); H=r['blind'].get('He3',{}).get('BE')
    A(f"| {k} | {row.get('mode','—')}/{row.get('form','—')} | {row['r']} | {K.DELTA_GRID[row['di']]:.4f} | {r['E0'] if r['E0'] is None else round(r['E0'],3)} | {r.get('e0',0):.3f} | {('%.3f'%r['E1']) if r['E1'] is not None else '—'} | {('%.3f'%last[1]) if last else '—'} | {('%.2f'%last[2]['dmin']) if last else '—'} | {('**%.3f**'%T) if T else '—'} | {('**%.3f**'%H) if H else '—'} | {r['stage']}{(': '+'; '.join(f for f in r['flags'] if 'stiff' not in f)) if r['flags'] and r['stage']=='dead' else ''} |")
    if r['stage']=='done': rowsout[k]=dict(T=T,He3=H,lam=r['E1'],r=row['r'],delta=K.DELTA_GRID[row['di']])
A(f"\nMeasured (compare.py, last section): T 8.482, ³He 7.718 MeV. Required per-bond after Y(2) slingshot, mesh and Coulomb: D 0.788, T 2.394, ³He 2.459, ⁴He 4.667 MeV → ratios T/D 3.04, ³He/D 3.12, ⁴He/D 5.92. Pure arithmetic of the lane factor (no geometry) predicts T/D = ³He/D = (1 + ⁴He/D)/2 = 3.46, i.e. T +14 %, ³He +11 %; the membrane's geometry moves it to the numbers above.\n")
an=R('analyse_v3.json')
A("## 3. Patch geometry at the row r = 0.3, δ = 0.168 (triplet/linear). E_patch is the raw e₀∫s dA (multiply by the lane factor for the actual adhesion).\n")
A("| state | pair | lane factor | d (fm) | E_patch raw | vertices | aspect | well−geom (hub +) | hub-half |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
lf={}
for k,r in st.items():
    if k=='r0.3_d1_kb0.2_triplet_linear':
        for n,v in r['blind'].items(): lf[n]=v['lane_factors']
        lf['He4']=[e for e in r['he4'] if e[1] is not None][-1][2]['lane_factors']
for n,tag in [('v3_r0.3_d1_kb0.2_triplet_linear_T','T'),('v3_r0.3_d1_kb0.2_triplet_linear_He3','He3'),('v3_r0.3_d1_kb0.2_triplet_linear_He4_lam_2.27675','He4')]:
    if n not in an: continue
    for k,v in an[n]['pairs'].items():
        key=k[0]+k[3]; A(f"| {tag} | {k} | {lf.get(tag,{}).get(key,'—')} | {v['d']:.3f} | {v['E_patch']:+.3f} | {v['n_vertices']} | {v['aspect']:.3f} | {v.get('well_minus_geom_hub',float('nan')):+.4f} | {v.get('hub_half_fraction',float('nan')):.3f} |")
A("\n**Readings.** (i) The same-species patch is the thin one in both T (nn: raw 0.431 vs 0.54, d 1.70 vs 1.62) and ³He (pp: 0.411, d 1.665) — P3 of the physics spec appears as a *consequence* of 'a singlet fuses no lane', not as an input. (ii) ⁴He is not a regular tetrahedron: np distances 1.49–1.56 fm, nn 1.73, pp 1.72 — squashed along the np bonds. (iii) Hub-half fractions 0.45–0.58, no consistent fat end at the hub: the egg ruling is still not reproduced.\n")
A("## 4. Pull-off profiles on the v3 triton (F = front width × line energy, raw e₀ line energy)\n")
f=os.path.join(HERE,'results','pulloff_v3_r0.3_d1_kb0.2_triplet_linear_T.json')
if os.path.exists(f):
    A("| pair | axisym F_max | ρ*/ρ_max | tinkle | tangential F_max | u* | tinkle |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
    for k,v in json.load(open(f)).items():
        ax=v['axisymmetric']; t=v['tangential']; ur=t['u_range']
        A(f"| {k} | {ax['F_max']:.3f} | {ax['rho_star']/ax['rho_max']:.2f} | {ax['tinkle_fraction']:.2f} | {t['F_max']:.3f} | {(t['u_star']-ur[0])/(ur[1]-ur[0]):.2f} | {t['tinkle_fraction']:.2f} |")
    A("\nDome world again: peaks at 0.54–0.62 of the radius, tinkle 0.34–0.48 (dome 0.58 / 0.44).\n")
A("## 5. Not run\n\nLoad paths, quartic mode, chain, SUBDIV 4 on the v3 states (time). The v2 pull-off/path cross-check (ratio 1.15 / 0.94) stands for the mechanism.\n")
A("## 6. Comparison with targets (compare.py — last)\n")
import compare
rows={}
for k,v in rowsout.items():
    rows[k]={'T':dict(BE=v['T'],Rch=an.get('v3_'+k+'_T',{}).get('Rch_classical',float('nan'))),'He3':dict(BE=v['He3'],Rch=an.get('v3_'+k+'_He3',{}).get('Rch_classical',float('nan')))}
A(compare.table(rows))
open(os.path.join(HERE,'report_v3.md'),'w').write("\n".join(L)+"\n"); print('report_v3.md written')
